  "text": "Settings\n\nPersonalize your launcher. Game settings belong to each instance.\n\nAppearance\nHome & Widgets\nLauncher\nMinecraft & Java\nUpdates\nDiscord & privacy\nAccessibility\nAbout\nDiscord & privacy\n\nYou decide which activity details appear on your Discord profile.\n\nDiscord\n\nOptional activity on your desktop Discord profile. No account link required.\n\nApplication setup required\nThis build needs Aurora’s Discord application registration before it can connect. Your preferences can still be saved.\nDiscord Rich Presence\nPublishes In Launcher, Starting Minecraft or Playing Minecraft. Turning off clears Aurora’s activity. Your detail preferences are kept while it is off.\nOff\nGame details\nMinecraft version\nThe exact installed game version.\nOff\nPlatform / loader\nThe installed platform and loader reported by Aurora.\nOff\nAurora Client active state\nVerified Aurora bootstrap active at launch; not a live client health signal.\nOff\nElapsed play time\nTime since the supervised game process started.\nOff\nInstance name\nShares your chosen instance name with Discord.\nOff\nWorld & server privacy\nShow World\nDisplays the singleplayer world’s name when a compatible Aurora Client reports it.\nOff\nShow Server\nDisplays the multiplayer server’s saved/display name when available.\nOff\nShow Server Address\nAlso allows the raw hostname/address to appear. Requires Show Server.\nOff\n\nWorld and server details require a compatible, active Aurora Client. Without its authenticated activity, Discord shows generic process activity.\n\nOff by default. All extra details require opt-in. Discord’s own activity visibility settings also apply. Connection problems never block Play.\n\nPreferences save as you change them. Game configuration uses Save changes in the instance workspace.",
